# A mana ability whose own cost is mana is paid out of the same pool the spell is being paid from, so it can take mana
# the player has already put towards the spell. Batroc the Leaper has a multikicker, which is what sends its payment
# down the "cost with X" path, where what is committed is tracked across the whole conversation rather than re-derived
# from the pool each time. Bot1 taps a Mountain for {R} towards Batroc's {R}, then sacrifices Chromatic Star for a
# white mana — whose own {1} spends that very {R}. The {R} must stop being committed when it leaves the pool: the cost
# owes it again, the second Mountain pays it, and Batroc is cast for {R} and {W} and not for a Red that is gone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Chromatic Star
Batroc the Leaper
Island x3
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chromatic Star.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Batroc the Leaper.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Chromatic Star.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Batroc the Leaper; Mountain; Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield.Batroc the Leaper.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Tapped = true
Bot1.Graveyard = Chromatic Star
Bot1.Mana = 
Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
